Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:08:03 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 126/126] contrib: fluidlite: take the loop of a compressed
 sample as a SoundFont 2 sample's

Once FluidLite has decoded a compressed (SF3) sample, it took the sample's
loop as broken, and replaced it with one from its ninth point to its ninth
before last, when the loop ended at the point after the sample's last or
started at the sample's first. A SoundFont 2 sample's loop may do both,
and FluidLite keeps both for an uncompressed sample. GeneralUser GS
converted to SF3 had 50 of its 920 loops moved, a grand piano's sustain
among them. Check a decoded sample's loop as an uncompressed one's is.
---
